course: dictionary
lesson: 2286
title: Crest: a top, a badge or a feather
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to find the right one. «The crest of the hill was covered in snow.» The hill and the snow tell you that crest means the top of the hill.
explain: The same word can name a feather or a badge. «The cockatoo raised its crest.» Here the crest is a bunch of feathers on its head. «The school crest is stitched on the blazer.» Here it is a special badge. Check by swapping in your meaning and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Crest can also be a verb, an action word. «The runners crested the hill and waved to their friends» means they reached the top. Phrases help too: «on the crest of a wave» means very successful at the moment.
fact: A crest can be a bunch of feathers, fur or skin on the top of an animal's head.
fact: «Cockatoos raise their crest feathers when excited or alarmed.»
fact: The crest of a hill or wave is its top, and the low point of a wave is its trough.
fact: A crest is also a special picture or badge of a family, school, team or town, as in «school crest».
fact: To crest means to reach the top, and «on the crest of a wave» means very successful at the moment.
exercise: «Cockatoos raise their crest feathers when excited or alarmed.» What is a crest here? | A steep path up a hill | The bottom of a wave | A school badge | *A bunch of feathers on the top of the head
exercise: «The crest of the hill was covered in snow.» What does crest mean? | A small stream at the bottom | The steep side of the hill | *The top of the hill | A school badge
exercise: «The family crest was painted on the shield.» What is a crest here? | *A special badge of a family | A bunch of feathers | To climb up | The top of a wave
test: «The surfer rode on the crest of the wave.» What does crest mean here? | A loud noise from the water | *The top of the wave | The sand at the bottom of the sea | A bunch of feathers
test: «The runners crested the hill and waved to their friends.» What does crested mean? | Fell down the slope | Stopped to rest at the bottom | Ran into the woods | *Reached the top
exam: Meera says, «She is on the crest of a wave since she won the race.» What does it mean? | She is very cold and wet | She is standing on a huge wave | She has lost her feathers | *Very successful at the moment
